==English==

===Etymology===
An [[Australianism]] where [[polly]] is derived from the term [[politician]] which is joined with the work [[speak]]. It is generally accepted as a [[derogatory]] term to describe political [[spin]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{slang|Australia}} A politician who [[spin]]s a political argument to win voter opinion.
# {{slang|Australia}} A politician who uses '''broad terms''' to describe an event, decision or action in an effort to avoid being committed to or held responsible for a given argument.

